  "question": "Evaluate $\\int \\sqrt{\\tan x} dx$.",
  "answeroption": "D",
  "explanation": "Let $\\sqrt{\\tan x}=t$ so $\\tan x=t^2$.<br /><br />Differentiating gives $\\sec^2 x dx=2t dt$.<br /><br />Thus $dx=\\frac{2t}{1+t^4}dt$.<br /><br />Integral becomes $2\\int\\frac{t^2}{1+t^4}dt$.<br /><br />After decomposition and integration the result becomes:<br /><br />$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt2}\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\tan x-1}{\\sqrt{2\\tan x}}\\right)+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt2}\\ln\\left|\\frac{\\tan x-\\sqrt{2\\tan x}+1}{\\tan x+\\sqrt{2\\tan x}+1}\\right|+C$.",
  "explanation_image": [],
